<title>NORWAY: Storebrand attracts foreign buyers.</title>
<headline>Storebrand attracts foreign buyers.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Overseas interest in Norway's largest insurance company Storebrand ASA was high on Friday and market players said one foreign buyer was looking to pick up a 10 percent stake in the group.</p>
<p>Turnover in Storebrand was a hefty 555 million crowns in Friday's session, with a large block of 8.32 million shares moving in a single off-exchange trade.</p>
<p>&quot;I have been in contact with a foreign broker, who has asked me to find large blocks of shares in Storebrand,&quot; said one dealer. &quot;He said there was one overseas investor who wants to buy up to 10 percent (in the company).&quot;</p>
<p>Storebrand closed 0.90 crowns up at 45.10 crowns.</p>
<p>--Steinar Dyrnes, Oslo newsroom +47 22 93 69 02</p>
